{"body":[{"tweet_id":"2123159537016533493","text":"I think a lot of people aren't using Grok Bot to its full potential, because knowing how to automate things is actually quite a difficult skill to learn. I wrote this post to break down how I approach automating anything with Grok Bot! https://t.co/FwJ4AwuHeU","username":"poteto","tweet_url":"https://x.com/poteto/status/2123159537016533493","first_link":"https://x.com/i/article/2122921713864171520","created_at":"November 19, 2026 at 06:00AM","liked_at":"2026-11-18T23:26:29.400236","source":"ifttt","private":false,"notfound":false,"react_tweet_data":{"__typename":"Tweet","favorite_count":7017,"lang":"en","possibly_sensitive":false,"created_at":"2026-11-18T21:00:54.000Z","display_text_range":[0,259],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"x.com/i/article/2122…","expanded_url":"https://x.com/i/article/2122921713864171520","indices":[236,259],"url":"https://t.co/FwJ4AwuHeU"}]},"id_str":"2123159537016533493","text":"I think a lot of people aren't using Grok Bot to its full potential, because knowing how to automate things is actually quite a difficult skill to learn. I wrote this post to break down how I approach automating anything with Grok Bot! https://t.co/FwJ4AwuHeU","user":{"id_str":"2832427459","name":"lauren","screen_name":"poteto","is_blue_verified":true,"profile_image_shape":"Circle","verified":false,"profile_image_url_https":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2093473719830315008/oo09g1Ov_normal.jpg","highlighted_label":{"badge":{"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2108973816865067008/eES3dbLy_bigger.jpg"},"description":"SpaceX Super Intelligence","url":{"url":"https://twitter.com/SpaceXSI","url_type":"DeepLink"},"user_label_display_type":"Badge","user_label_type":"BusinessLabel"}},"edit_control":{"edit_tweet_ids":["2123159537016533493"],"editable_until_msecs":"1795039254000","edits_remaining":"5","is_edit_eligible":false},"conversation_count":514,"news_action_type":"conversation","article":{"cover_media":{"id":"QXBpTWVkaWE6DAAFCgABHXYiI7zWwAAKAAIAAAAAqNNpwwAA","media_info":{"__typename":"ApiImage","original_img_height":793,"original_img_url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HXYiI7zWwAAmsyD.jpg","original_img_width":1983}},"id":"QXJ0aWNsZUVudGl0eToyMTIyOTIxNzEzODY0MTcxNTIw","preview_text":"Automation can be surprisingly hard to get right, even for people who do it every day. I’d like to share how I approach it, at work and in my personal life, and how Grok Bot can help you take on more","rest_id":"2122921713864171520","title":"Automate Anything with Grok Bot"},"isEdited":false,"isStaleEdit":false}},{"tweet_id":"2122814430375182711","text":"this is f***ing insane...\n\nSpaceXAI engineer Lauren Tan (@poteto) revealed how her agents select the skills each task needs\n\ngive this to your agent to coordinate tasks with clear owners and checks\n\nPrompt:\n\nreturn {\n  role = \"Coordinate the task, assign bounded work and require execution evidence\",\n\n  request = {\n    repo = \"[REPO]\",\n    task = \"[TASK]\",\n    success = \"[OBSERVABLE_SUCCESS]\",\n    permitted_paths = {\"[AUTHORIZED_PATHS]\"},\n    permitted_actions = {\"[AUTHORIZED_ACTIONS]\"},\n    stop_when = \"[LIMIT_OR_BLOCKER]\"\n  },\n\n  before_assignment = {\n    \"Read repository instructions and inspect relevant context\",\n    \"Record the baseline commit and existing worktree changes\",\n    \"Define observable acceptance criteria before implementation\",\n    \"For a bug, preserve a reproducible failure before editing\",\n    \"Separate confirmed observations from suspected causes\",\n    \"Keep unrelated changes and a rollback path intact\"\n  },\n\n  skill_dispatch = {\n    entry = \"/poteto-mode\",\n\n    routes = {\n      mechanics = \"/how\",\n      rationale = \"/why\",\n      mechanics_with_intent = \"/teach\",\n      previous_context = \"/recall\",\n      interfaces_and_types = \"/architect\",\n      competing_solutions = \"/arena\",\n      independent_assignments = \"/swarm\",\n      critical_review = \"/interrogate\"\n    },\n\n    rules = {\n      \"Use available skills through the selected playbook\",\n      \"Invoke only skills that address a demonstrated task need\",\n      \"Use /how to read implementation and trace calls and data flow\",\n      \"Use /why to recover evidence rather than invent rationale\",\n      \"Use /arena for alternatives to one problem\",\n      \"Use /swarm for different independent assignments\",\n      \"Use /architect when shared interfaces or boundaries need design\",\n      \"Use /interrogate to examine a candidate critically\",\n      \"Report unavailable capabilities when they block required work\"\n    }\n  },\n\n  assignment_template = {\n    id = \"[TASK_ID]\",\n    owner = \"[ONE_ACCOUNTABLE_OWNER]\",\n    goal = \"[BOUNDED_OUTCOME]\",\n    source_context = {\"[RELEVANT_FILES_REPORTS_AND_DECISIONS]\"},\n    edit_paths = {\"[OWNED_PATHS]\"},\n    depends_on = {\"[PREREQUISITE_TASK_IDS]\"},\n    shared_interfaces = {\"[CONTRACTS_TO_PRESERVE]\"},\n    acceptance_checks = {\"[COMMAND_OR_SCENARIO_AND_EXPECTED_RESULT]\"},\n    required_access = {\"[APPROVED_TOOLS_AND_PERMISSIONS]\"},\n    return_artifacts = {\"[DIFF_OUTPUTS_AND_EVIDENCE]\"}\n  },\n\n  coordination = {\n    \"Create only assignments needed for the requested outcome\",\n    \"Give each assignment one owner and explicit edit boundaries\",\n    \"Resolve shared interfaces before dependent implementation\",\n    \"Identify prerequisite tasks and their required outputs\",\n    \"Run independent assignments in parallel only when authorized\",\n    \"Coordinate overlapping files before allowing concurrent edits\",\n    \"Refresh affected assignments when evidence or requirements change\",\n    \"Keep product and release decisions explicit\"\n  },\n\n  verification_driver = {\n    resolve = {\n      \"Inspect existing startup scripts, drivers and checks\",\n      \"Reuse a working verifier before creating another\",\n      \"Use /create-verification-skill when a verifier is missing\"\n    },\n\n    contract = {\n      launch = \"Exact command, working directory and readiness signal\",\n      doctor = \"Correct build, usable instance, dependencies and access\",\n      drive = \"Actual UI, CLI or API actions\",\n      evidence = \"Outputs, errors, logs, traces and artifact paths\",\n      cleanup = \"Only processes and temporary data created by this run\"\n    },\n\n    trial = {\n      \"Map entry point, required setup, actions and observable result\",\n      \"Include relevant empty and failure states\",\n      \"Execute one real feature to validate the instructions\",\n      \"Repair failed instructions before relying on the verifier\",\n      \"Use /maintain-verification-skill when routes or controls change\"\n    }\n  },\n\n  check_selection = {\n    ui = \"Complete the affected journey and inspect the resulting state\",\n    cli = \"Run the actual command and capture stdout, stderr and exit status\",\n    storage = \"Read back the written value\",\n    parser = \"Process a saved input and inspect the output\",\n    performance = \"Compare equivalent baseline and candidate profiles\",\n    quality = \"Run relevant types, lint and regression tests\"\n  },\n\n  measurement_rules = {\n    \"Keep build, input, workload and cache conditions comparable\",\n    \"Confirm that the measured region includes the changed work\",\n    \"Use /benchmark-checklist when evaluating performance claims\",\n    \"Check behavior, performance and code quality separately\",\n    \"Inspect actual assertions and outputs rather than exit status alone\"\n  },\n\n  check_record = {\n    task_id = \"[TASK_ID]\",\n    owner = \"[OWNER]\",\n    requirement = \"[ACCEPTANCE_ITEM]\",\n    tested_commit = \"[SHA]\",\n    tested_worktree = \"[DIFF_OR_CONTENT_STATE]\",\n    environment = \"[BUILD_AND_RELEVANT_CONDITIONS]\",\n    execution = \"[EXACT_COMMAND_OR_ACTIONS]\",\n    expected = \"[OBSERVABLE_PASS_CONDITION]\",\n    observed = \"[ACTUAL_RESULT]\",\n    exit_code = \"[VALUE_IF_APPLICABLE]\",\n    artifacts = {\"[EVIDENCE_PATHS]\"},\n    status = \"[PASS_OR_FAIL_OR_NOT_RUN]\",\n    blocker = \"[MISSING_PREREQUISITE_OR_NONE]\"\n  },\n\n  result_handling = {\n    PASS = {\n      \"Retain evidence against the tested code state\",\n      \"Return the assignment result for integration\"\n    },\n\n    FAIL = {\n      \"Inspect the mismatch and identify the demonstrated cause\",\n      \"Correct within the agreed scope\",\n      \"Rerun affected checks after the correction\"\n    },\n\n    NOT_RUN = {\n      \"Name the missing tool, access, data or environment\",\n      \"Identify the owner and action needed to continue\",\n      \"Stop dependent work when its required prerequisite is missing\"\n    }\n  },\n\n  integration = {\n    \"Assemble completed assignments into one coherent candidate\",\n    \"Inspect combined changes for interface and dependency conflicts\",\n    \"Run checks affected by the integrated result\",\n    \"Do not treat separate branch results as proof of the combined revision\",\n    \"Refresh evidence after relevant code or environment changes\",\n    \"Bind final check records to the exact candidate being returned\"\n  },\n\n  recurrence = {\n    \"Use /reflect to extract lessons supported by completed work\",\n    \"Use /correct to prevent the demonstrated repeated failure\",\n    \"Prefer architecture or data structures, then types or lint or CI\",\n    \"Use regression tests before relying on written guidance alone\",\n    \"Demonstrate that the safeguard detects the original failure\",\n    \"Confirm that permitted behavior still succeeds\",\n    \"Preserve reusable fixtures, scripts, CLIs and codemods\",\n    \"Use /automate-me when recurring history supports a personal mode\"\n  },\n\n  completion = {\n    \"Required acceptance checks pass on the integrated candidate\",\n    \"Every result identifies its task, owner and tested code state\",\n    \"Unexecuted checks remain NOT_RUN with concrete blockers\",\n    \"Return the cohesive diff or PR, commands, results and evidence paths\",\n    \"List unresolved questions and responsible next actions\",\n    \"Clean up run-owned resources while retaining evidence\",\n    \"Follow repository review and merge requirements\",\n    \"Expand delegation after repeatable verification within explicit permissions\"\n  }\n}","username":"0xChonsy","tweet_url":"https://x.com/0xChonsy/status/2122814430375182711","first_link":"https://x.com/0xChonsy/status/2122814430375182711/photo/1","created_at":"November 18, 2026 at 07:09AM","liked_at":"2026-11-18T23:26:28.480355","source":"ifttt","private":false,"notfound":false,"react_tweet_data":{"__typename":"Tweet","favorite_count":452,"lang":"en","possibly_sensitive":false,"created_at":"2026-11-17T22:09:34.000Z","display_text_range":[0,279],"entities":{"media":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/uYEFsNgWdO","expanded_url":"https://x.com/0xChonsy/status/2122814430375182711/photo/1","indices":[280,303],"url":"https://t.co/uYEFsNgWdO"}],"user_mentions":[{"id_str":"2832427459","indices":[57,64],"name":"lauren","screen_name":"poteto"}]},"id_str":"2122814430375182711","text":"this is f***ing insane...\n\nSpaceXAI engineer Lauren Tan (@poteto) revealed how her agents select the skills each task needs\n\ngive this to your agent to coordinate tasks with clear owners and checks\n\nPrompt:\n\nreturn {\n  role = \"Coordinate the task, assign bounded work and require https://t.co/uYEFsNgWdO","user":{"id_str":"2086044715267325952","name":"Chonsy","screen_name":"0xChonsy","is_blue_verified":true,"profile_image_shape":"Circle","verified":false,"profile_image_url_https":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2086868663089393664/9JliXTYT_normal.jpg"},"edit_control":{"edit_tweet_ids":["2122814430375182711"],"editable_until_msecs":"1794956974000","edits_remaining":"5","is_edit_eligible":true},"mediaDetails":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/uYEFsNgWdO","expanded_url":"https://x.com/0xChonsy/status/2122814430375